Yes, and remember that sacrificing will help reducing prayer timeout.

These things reduce prayer timeout:
Time passing (-1 per turn)
Sacrificing on aligned altar (varies, depends on monster value, chaotics 
get 5/3 times better value than others)

These things set your prayer timeout:
Starting a new character (300)
Angering your god (rnz(300))
Praying (rnz(350))
Getting an artifact gift from a sacrifice (rnz(300+50*number of 
artifacts generated in the dungeon))

These things add to your prayer timeout:
Praying while being crowned (rnz(1000))
Praying if killed Yendor or performed the ritual (rnz(1000))
If both above are true (2*rnz(1000))
Permanent change of alignment (300)
Praying too soon (rnz(250))
Doing water prayer on non-coaligned altar (rnz(250))
Getting a wish fullfilled (rn1(100,50))


Prayer timeout is never negative.

